11
00:00:42,719 --> 00:00:51,039
Debouncing works like this: when

12
00:00:46,280 --> 00:00:55,039
you use a push button in many places,

13
00:00:51,039 --> 00:00:58,719
in every device, for example in a washing machine,

14
00:00:55,039 --> 00:01:01,879
a refrigerator, or a hood, sometimes these

15
00:00:58,719 --> 00:01:05,680
push buttons are touch buttons,

16
00:01:01,879 --> 00:01:09,920
and sometimes they are physical push buttons.

17
00:01:05,680 --> 00:01:12,280
In any case, we need to solve

18
00:01:09,920 --> 00:01:14,400
the debouncing problem that exists in them.

19
00:01:12,280 --> 00:01:17,799
What is this problem? The problem is that

20
00:01:14,400 --> 00:01:19,960
when you press a button,

21
00:01:17,799 --> 00:01:23,240


22
00:01:19,960 --> 00:01:26,680
Imagine this is a button and you are

23
00:01:23,240 --> 00:01:30,840
pressing this button. It causes

24
00:01:26,680 --> 00:01:34,600
the contact on the push button

25
00:01:30,840 --> 00:01:36,920
to actually, over a period of

26
00:01:34,600 --> 00:01:40,640
about 30 milliseconds, 40 milliseconds,

27
00:01:36,920 --> 00:01:42,720
or 50 milliseconds, bounce several times.

28
00:01:40,640 --> 00:01:45,159
You press it once, but

29
00:01:42,720 --> 00:01:49,840
the contact bounces and causes the

30
00:01:45,159 --> 00:01:52,479
LED to turn on and off four times, for example.

31
00:01:49,840 --> 00:01:54,840
Or suppose you want a value, a number,

32
00:01:52,479 --> 00:01:56,840
to increase once by pressing a button,

33
00:01:54,840 --> 00:01:59,560
but you see it increasing four times

34
00:01:56,840 --> 00:02:03,079
in a row. That is why it

35
00:01:59,560 --> 00:02:06,560
can cause problems, because in industry

36
00:02:03,079 --> 00:02:10,080
this debouncing issue can be very

37
00:02:06,560 --> 00:02:13,120
troublesome, and we need to find a solution for it.

38
00:02:10,080 --> 00:02:17,080
In this session, we want to press

39
00:02:13,120 --> 00:02:20,760
a key and increase the number shown on the seven-segment

40
00:02:17,080 --> 00:02:25,760
display once for each press,

41
00:02:20,760 --> 00:02:25,760
so the number on the seven-segment increases once.

42
00:02:26,519 --> 00:02:34,280
So, I explained what debouncing is and said that

43
00:02:31,800 --> 00:02:37,840
mechanically, what problems

44
00:02:34,280 --> 00:02:40,080
it creates and its solution. Here I will explain it.

45
00:02:37,840 --> 00:02:43,840
There are two solutions. One is

46
00:02:40,080 --> 00:02:45,800
to use, in a hardware approach,

47
00:02:43,840 --> 00:02:50,480
an RC circuit

48
00:02:45,800 --> 00:02:53,560
to eliminate the debouncing of the push button.

49
00:02:50,480 --> 00:02:55,879
However, the circuit becomes more complicated,

50
00:02:53,560 --> 00:02:58,280
and if you want to try a circuit

51
00:02:55,879 --> 00:03:00,040
in mass production, you have to add

52
00:02:58,280 --> 00:03:03,360
some components to the circuit.

53
00:03:00,040 --> 00:03:06,640
This increases the cost and can make the error

54
00:03:03,360 --> 00:03:08,560
greater than in the software approach.

55
00:03:06,640 --> 00:03:11,440
In the software approach,

56
00:03:08,560 --> 00:03:13,200
we use programming

57
00:03:11,440 --> 00:03:16,400
to solve the problem.

58
00:03:13,200 --> 00:03:19,640
It practically solves the debouncing problem

59
00:03:16,400 --> 00:03:23,680
so that when we press once, only one event

60
00:03:19,640 --> 00:03:25,920
